 Friendship Games competition, held a week after the Olympics, with a total weight of 252.5 kg, which would have easily won him the Olympic gold. Of the active competitors, only " [:a {:href "/athletes/56189"} "Kazushito Manabe"] " had medalled before internationally, having claimed bronze at the 1981 World Championships. At the 1983 Moscow Worlds, he had been 5th."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In competition, Manabe would be challenged by two Chinese lifters, the first to compete since the 1936 Berlin Games. " [:a {:href "/athletes/55408"} "Zhou Peishun"] " had been 7th in the Moscow World Championships, but he was challenged by his 19-year-old countryman, " [:a {:href "/athletes/55403"} "Zeng Guoqiang"] ". While trailing Zhou after the snatch, Zeng made up the difference in the clean &amp; jerk. As both Chinese lifters were tied, the winner was Zeng, who had weighed in at 51.70 kg, 0.1 kg less than Zhou."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Fourth place finisher " [:a {:href "/athletes/56315"} "Mahmoud Tarha"] " of Lebanon was later disqualified after it was found he had used the forbidden substance nandrolone."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55403"} "Zeng Guoqiang"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "235.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55408"} "Zhou Peishun"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "235.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :styl